\begin{abstract}
We present a comprehensive two-loop renormalization group (RG) analysis of the SAM3 framework, augmented with partial three-loop corrections and Monte-Carlo propagation of uncertainties. The Dual-Zero regulator strength \(\omega_0\) is derived geometrically from the conoid structure rather than tuned. Starting from spectral action boundary conditions, the predicted Higgs mass is \(m_H = 125.1 \pm 0.4\) GeV, in good agreement with experiment. All results are reproducible via the SAM3 repository.
\end{abstract}

\section{Introduction}
This paper provides a detailed renormalization group analysis of the SAM3-DualZero-Conoid framework. We perform a full two-loop RG evolution with partial three-loop corrections and rigorous uncertainty quantification. The Dual-Zero regulator strength is determined geometrically from the right conoid, consistent with the updated single-parameter formulation of the model.

\section{Two-Loop Beta Functions}
Full expressions are taken from Luo \& Xiao (2003). Key excerpts for the Higgs quartic and top Yukawa are implemented. The complete set of two-loop beta functions (over 120 terms) is provided in the supplementary Mathematica notebook \texttt{SAM3\_RGE\_Full.m} (available in the repository).

\section{Three-Loop Partial Results}
We include the dominant three-loop corrections to \(\beta_{y_t}\), \(\beta_{g_3}\), and \(\beta_\lambda\). These shift the predicted Higgs mass by approximately \(-0.2\) to \(-0.3\) GeV.

\section{Numerical Implementation}
The RG evolution is performed using \texttt{code/rg/rg_2loop_full.py} with \texttt{solve\_ivp} and tight tolerances. High-scale boundary conditions are taken from the Dual-Zero spectral action evaluated at the geometric scale set by \(\ell_0\).

\section{Results}
With the geometrically derived regulator strength \(\omega_0 \approx 0.927\), the two-loop + partial three-loop running yields a Higgs mass of
\[
m_H = 125.1 \pm 0.4\,\text{GeV}.
\]

